***************************** T A L Y S **************************1837 1451  185
                                                                  1837 1451  186
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   1837 1451  187
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      1837 1451  188
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    1837 1451  189
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     1837 1451  190
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  1837 1451  191
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        1837 1451  192
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    1837 1451  193
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         1837 1451  194
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      1837 1451  195
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    1837 1451  196
stored in this data file:                                         1837 1451  197
                                                                  1837 1451  198
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   1837 1451  199
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     1837 1451  200
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 1837 1451  201
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   1837 1451  202
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                1837 1451  203
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   1837 1451  204
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    1837 1451  205
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        1837 1451  206
- Recoil data                                                     1837 1451  207
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           1837 1451  208
- Total particle energy spectra                                   1837 1451  209
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      1837 1451  210
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        1837 1451  211
- Residual production cross sections                              1837 1451  212
                                                                  1837 1451  213
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            1837 1451  214
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        1837 1451  215
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   1837 1451  216
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                1837 1451  217
                                                                  1837 1451  218
